---
<PageLayout
  title="Uniforms"
  description="Class A, B, and C uniform requirements for Trail Life Troop TX-0521."
  heading="Uniforms"
  heroImage="/images/uniforms-hero.jpg"
  heroAlt="River surrounded by forests under a cloudy sky"
>
  <Section tone="light" class="narrow-content">
    <p class="scripture">
      "The uniform makes for brotherhood, since when universally adopted it covers up all differences of class and country."
      <cite>Lord Robert Baden-Powell</cite>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream" class="uniform-classes">
    <HotspotImage src="/images/oathboy-uniform.png" alt="Trailman in the Class A uniform" width={364} height={896} hotspots={hotspots} />
    <div>
      <h2>Class A Uniform</h2>
      <h3>Formal &ndash; <em>Required</em></h3>
      <p>This formal uniform is required for all troop meetings, ceremonies, parades, and dress occasions. It consists of a class A uniform shirt, shoulder loops, troop numeral/state patch, lanyard with ID, and tri-color Trail Life hat.</p>
      <p>Trailmen <strong>should</strong> wear appropriate pants or shorts that are khaki or dark in color (black/navy or jeans). Styles may include cargo, jeans, or similar. We kindly ask that you do <strong><u>not</u></strong> wear athletic pants or shorts, including gym shorts.</p>
      <p>Trailmen <strong>should not</strong> wear torn or otherwise defaced or altered uniforms and should be neat in appearance.</p>
      <p>Closed-toed shoes are required.</p>
      <p><a href="https://shop.traillifeusa.com/product/troop-uniform-build-your-own-bundle" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Troop Uniform Bundle</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="https://shop.traillifeusa.com/product/tri-color-hat" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Tri-Color Hat</a></p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="light" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Class B &amp; Class C</h2>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid-2">
      <Card variant="surface">
        <h3>Class B Uniform</h3>
        <p class="uniform-tag">Travel &ndash; Optional</p>
        <p>This travel uniform is a Trail Life USA official polo, purchased from the Trail Life store. If a Trailman decides to wear this uniform, it must match his current program (Woodlands Trail, Navigators, or Adventurers).</p>
      </Card>
      <Card variant="surface">
        <h3>Class C Uniform</h3>
        <p class="uniform-tag">Trail &ndash; Coming Soon</p>
        <p>This trail uniform is ideal for outdoor adventures where it isn't as practical to wear the formal or travel uniforms. Any Trail Life USA official t-shirts are acceptable. Troop TX-0521 is in the process of getting t-shirts specifically for our troop.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</PageLayout>
